      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T15:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So here you run into an empty line and send it off to the skottie shaper as an empty line. `shapeLine` the notices that this is empty and then calls `beginLine` and `commitLine`. The `commitLine` keeps track of the line count in `ResultBuilder::fLineCount`. (The line count was already being kept in the ResultBuilder.) `commitLine` when it outputs things (which creates fragments) passes along the current line so that the fragment is aware of the line it is on. This change then puts this `ResultBuilder::fLineCount` into the new `skottie::Shaper::Result::fLineCount`.\n\nThis change (at PS9) then uses this information by going over the fragments and adding in any lines missing, using `skottie::Shaper::Result::fLineCount` to know how many might be missing at the end.\n\nI was going to suggest that maybe the when building the result that there be an extra `addEmptyLine` which could be called here which adds the empty fragment. I suppose that\u0027s a bit less performant since it would need to be created, but I think would simplify things since then there would be a fragment for every line.",
      "revId": "aae771729ddaaca0bbab954c25886e6bfcba1dd6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
